 "_fence_note": "What part of the watched channels and repos is the user's. keywords: plain words that make a text in-fence. alert_re, text_re: a pattern of the install's own for alerts and for messages (they win over keywords). paths: repo -> path prefixes (paths_re: repo -> a pattern for single files outside them). patrol_areas: [repo, folder] pairs read in rotation. stop_words: words too common here to tell two pieces of work apart (a list, or a list per use: epics, merge_order, precedents). All empty: everything watched is in scope.",
 "fence": {"keywords": [], "paths": {}, "paths_re": {}, "patrol_areas": [], "stop_words": [], "alert_re": "", "text_re": ""},
 "_checks_note": "repos.<name>.checks: what the gate runs for that repo, a list of {name, run, dir, paths, timeout_s, setup}. run is a shell command from dir (the repo root when unset); {files} in it becomes the changed files under dir; paths (prefixes) make it run only when the diff touches them; setup runs once before, in dir. Unset: the gate detects checks from the repo's own files. An empty list: no checks. quality.check_timeout_s is the default time limit of each one.",
